  "_comment": "Signature-block detection terms, organized by concept and language. `und` is reserved for structural markers or name/legal tokens that are not tied to the document language. `signatureStampPhrases` are the fixed strings PDF signing software stamps onto a page; a person span must never extend across one. `personListLabels`, `personListLabelOmissions`, and `contactFieldLabels` form the reviewed coverage matrix for every manifest language. Labels are native legal notice or procurement conventions, not translated guesses. A person-list label activates only beside a semicolon-delimited list or a configured contact field. `personValueLabels` contains only labels whose value is a person's name; broader `formFieldLabels` also contains organization, role, date, address, and tax fields and must not be used to introduce a person.",
